  "id": 0,
  "name": "kthread",
  "doc": "Lifecycle of one guest thread in the kernel (src/kernel). Created is the slot while CreateThread fills it in; Dormant is a published thread before StartThread. A pause is a state: a thread that is waiting keeps its wait under it (PausedWaiting carries the same wait kind, PausedContending is a paused Contending), and it takes effect at a scheduling point: with green threads every thread but the caller of SetThreadActivity is at one, so a running thread of another core goes straight to PausedRunnable. Contending is a condition-variable waiter that was signalled while its mutex was held: it now waits for that lock. Terminate is process teardown and leaves every state but Created.",
  "states": ["Created", "Dormant", "Runnable", "Running", "Waiting", "Contending", "PausedDormant", "PausedRunnable", "PausedWaiting", "PausedContending", "Exited"],
  "initial": "Created",
